Input: {"question": "Which award did Victorine Raibaut receive?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 91, "text": "**Heroism in the Face of Horror: Victorine Raibaut Honored as Righteous Among the Nations**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 93, "end": 289, "text": "In a poignant tribute to her bravery and selflessness, Victorine Raibaut, a French woman, has been posthumously awarded the prestigious title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 290, "end": 438, "text": "This esteemed honor is bestowed upon non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews during the Holocaust, one of the darkest periods in human history."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 439, "end": 569, "text": "Raibaut's remarkable story of courage and compassion has come to light through the tireless efforts of historians and researchers."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 570, "end": 715, "text": "According to records, Raibaut, a resident of Lyon, France, provided shelter and protection to several Jewish families during the Nazi occupation."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 716, "end": 790, "text": "Her actions, though perilous, ensured the survival of many innocent lives."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 791, "end": 896, "text": "\"Victorine Raibaut's heroism is a shining example of humanity in the face of unimaginable evil,\" said Dr."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 897, "end": 964, "text": "Deborah Lipstadt, a renowned historian and expert on the Holocaust."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 965, "end": 1101, "text": "\"Her selfless acts of kindness and bravery serve as a powerful reminder of the importance of standing up against hatred and oppression.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1102, "end": 1163, "text": "Raibaut's bravery was not limited to providing shelter alone."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1164, "end": 1288, "text": "She also assisted in the distribution of false identification papers, food, and other essential supplies to those in hiding."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1289, "end": 1365, "text": "Her actions, though clandestine, were instrumental in saving numerous lives."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1366, "end": 1512, "text": "\"Victorine Raibaut's courage and generosity inspired others to follow in her footsteps,\" said Serge Klarsfeld, a French historian and Nazi hunter."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1513, "end": 1621, "text": "\"Her legacy serves as a testament to the power of individual action in the face of overwhelming oppression.\""}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1622, "end": 1741, "text": "The Righteous Among the Nations award, established in 1963, is a formal recognition of Raibaut's extraordinary heroism."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1742, "end": 1843, "text": "To date, over 26,000 individuals from more than 50 countries have been honored with this distinction."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1844, "end": 2050, "text": "According to data from Yad Vashem, the World Holocaust Remembrance Center, Raibaut's actions are a testament to the bravery of many ordinary people who risked everything to save others during the Holocaust."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2051, "end": 2236, "text": "In France alone, over 3,500 individuals have been recognized as Righteous Among the Nations, highlighting the significant role played by French citizens in rescuing Jews during the war."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2237, "end": 2378, "text": "Raibaut's story serves as a powerful reminder of the importance of promoting tolerance, understanding, and humanity in the face of adversity."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "**Victorine Raibaut**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 23, "end": 192, "text": "Victorine Raibaut was a French humanitarian and tourism advocate who was recognized for her outstanding contributions to the development of sustainable tourism in Spain."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 193, "end": 357, "text": "Born on February 12, 1925, in Lyon, France, Raibaut dedicated her life to promoting cross-cultural understanding and preserving the rich cultural heritage of Spain."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 358, "end": 383, "text": "**Early Life and Career**"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 385, "end": 525, "text": "Raibaut's fascination with Spanish culture began at a young age, inspired by her parents' stories of their travels to the Iberian Peninsula."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 526, "end": 729, "text": "She pursued a degree in Spanish literature from the University of Lyon, where she honed her language skills and developed a deep appreciation for the works of Spanish authors such as Cervantes and Lorca."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 730, "end": 846, "text": "After completing her studies, Raibaut moved to Madrid, where she worked as a cultural attaché at the French Embassy."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 847, "end": 1018, "text": "Her role involved promoting French-Spanish cultural exchange programs, which led to the establishment of several cultural centers and language institutes throughout Spain."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1019, "end": 1040, "text": "**Humanitarian Work**"}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1042, "end": 1173, "text": "Raibaut's humanitarian work began in the 1960s, when she founded the non-profit organization \"Amigos de España\" (Friends of Spain)."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1174, "end": 1309, "text": "The organization aimed to provide aid to rural communities in Spain, focusing on education, healthcare, and infrastructure development."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1310, "end": 1467, "text": "Raibaut's tireless efforts led to the construction of several schools, hospitals, and community centers, earning her recognition from the Spanish government."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1468, "end": 1500, "text": "**Gold Medal for Tourism Merit**"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1502, "end": 1692, "text": "In 1985, Raibaut was awarded the Gold Medal for Tourism Merit, a prestigious Spanish civil decoration, in recognition of her contributions to the development of sustainable tourism in Spain."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1693, "end": 1884, "text": "The award, conferred by King Juan Carlos I, acknowledged Raibaut's efforts in promoting eco-friendly tourism practices, preserving Spain's cultural heritage, and supporting local communities."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1885, "end": 1911, "text": "**Studies and References**"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1913, "end": 1987, "text": "* \"The Impact of Sustainable Tourism on Rural Development in Spain\" by Dr."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1988, "end": 2032, "text": "María Rodríguez, University of Madrid (1982)"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2033, "end": 2115, "text": "* \"Victorine Raibaut: A Life Dedicated to Spanish-French Cultural Exchange\" by Dr."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2116, "end": 2156, "text": "Pierre Dupont, University of Lyon (1995)"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2157, "end": 2229, "text": "* \"Amigos de España: A Study of Humanitarian Work in Rural Spain\" by Dr."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2230, "end": 2272, "text": "Juan Gómez, University of Barcelona (2001)"}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2274, "end": 2284, "text": "**Legacy**"}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2286, "end": 2410, "text": "Victorine Raibaut's legacy continues to inspire generations of tourism professionals, humanitarians, and cultural advocates."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Victorine Raibaut", "scope": "Award received", "claim": "Victorine Raibaut was posthumously awarded the title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel.", "answer": "Righteous Among the Nations", "quote": "In a poignant tribute to her bravery and selflessness, Victorine Raibaut, a French woman, has been posthumously awarded the prestigious title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel. This esteemed honor is bestowed upon non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews during the Holocaust, one of the darkest periods in human history. Raibaut's remarkable story of courage and compassion has come to light through the tireless efforts of historians and researchers. According to records, Raibaut, a resident of Lyon, France, provided shelter and protection to several Jewish families during the Nazi occupation. Her actions, though perilous, ensured the survival of many innocent lives. \"Victorine Raibaut's heroism is a shining example of humanity in the face of unimaginable evil,\" said Dr. Deborah Lipstadt, a renowned historian and expert on the Holocaust. \"Her selfless acts of kindness and bravery serve as a powerful reminder of the importance of standing up against hatred and oppression.\" Raibaut's bravery was not limited to providing shelter alone. She also assisted in the distribution of false identification papers, food, and other essential supplies to those in hiding. Her actions, though clandestine, were instrumental in saving numerous lives. \"Victorine Raibaut's courage and generosity inspired others to follow in her footsteps,\" said Serge Klarsfeld, a French historian and Nazi hunter. \"Her legacy serves as a testament to the power of individual action in the face of overwhelming oppression.\" The Righteous Among the Nations award, established in 1963, is a formal recognition of Raibaut's extraordinary heroism.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Victorine Raibaut", "scope": "Award received in 1985", "claim": "In 1985, Raibaut was awarded the Gold Medal for Tourism Merit, a prestigious Spanish civil decoration, in recognition of her contributions to the development of sustainable tourism in Spain.", "answer": "Gold Medal for Tourism Merit", "quote": "In 1985, Raibaut was awarded the Gold Medal for Tourism Merit, a prestigious Spanish civil decoration, in recognition of her contributions to the development of sustainable tourism in Spain. The award, conferred by King Juan Carlos I, acknowledged Raibaut's efforts in promoting eco-friendly tourism practices, preserving Spain's cultural heritage, and supporting local communities.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Righteous Among the Nations", "Gold Medal for Tourism Merit"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Righteous Among the Nations", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Gold Medal for Tourism Merit", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}

